entries.Goblin_Burner.description = Coming too close to the flame does...<i>things</i> to a Goblin.\n\nThough many believe it will bring them closer to those they seek to imitate, the temperament of the burners would indicate otherwise.
entries.Goblin_Feastmaster.description = Not all Goblin fascinations lead equally to greatness. To those who don the title of Feastmaster, recreating lost cuisine is their calling. Perhaps in the perfect recipe hides the path they seek, to the great flames of the civilization that inspired them.\n\nThat is, were they not prone to discarding their few edible dishes.
entries.Goblin_Glutton.description = These hulking brutes are foremost amongst a Feastmaster's chosen followers, though it is not in pursuit of the same goals they grow to such a size. Every Feastmaster needs a poison tester. Or two. Or twenty.\n\nThough who can say what a Goblin would consider to be poison?
entries.Goblin_Gobliterator.description = Despite its name, it seems unlikely the Makinomagistra intended this contraption to be a tool of destruction, though the scrappers she left behind after her escape must have believed otherwise.\n\nHer sense for naming is...unusual, even by Goblin standards.
entries.Goblin_Guardian.description = Toppled statues buried in the rubble of many a town provide an endless source of inspiration for the Goblin guardians.\n\nTheir poor condition only serves to further confuse the forms these guardians mimic. Yet still they choose to stand, defending the ruins of a civilization that couldn't save itself.
entries.Goblin_Lobber.description = Many Goblins take different paths in their search for the great flame.\n\nTo the lobbers, each bomb is a small rehearsal and a chance that maybe - just maybe - its blast will be as grand as the one spoken of in legends.
entries.Goblin_Miner.description = Mining is one of the few aspects of ancient Goblin civilization to have survived the cultural shift brought on by the Dukes' fascinations.\n\nIt's unfortunate that today's Goblins lack the fundamental understanding of the art their ancestors possessed.
entries.Goblin_Scientist.description = Only those whose obsession with technology surpasses even that of the stigmatized Enkindled engineers choose to don the title "Makinomagistra".\n\nThe current holder is known for her fascination with the derelict Ancient Gateways found in Orbis' oldest ruins. As the first Goblin to manage to escape Orbis through her own inventions, she has shown an uncharacteristic degree of success for a Duke.\n\nPerhaps her critical failure lies in the origins of the fascination itself.
entries.Goblin_Scrapper.description = Chaos given physical form.\n\nWhen a new Goblin dons the title of a Duke, the scrappers are the first to be drawn in by their obsession and often the cause of its premature end.
entries.Skeleton_Elite.description = The term "Guardian" was once synonymous with safety to towns and villages throughout Orbis, and the elite amongst their numbers were revered by the populace for generations. It was in part through their valor that the Great War was won - though even they were powerless in the face of what followed.
